{"There are two self.downsize method definitions where the latter overrides the former and changes the signature, which will raise ArgumentError for callers still passing max_width, max_height (e.g. app/jobs/regular/resize_emoji.rb)": 0.9501805305480957, "Hardcoding maxSizeKB to 10MB ignores the per-type max_*_size_kb site settings, so the client can accept files the server rejects or reject files when admins allow >10MB": 0.9903102517127991, "The downsize loop only shrinks to ~33% of the original after 5 iterations (0.8^5), so a 10MB image may still exceed max_image_size_kb and proceed to Upload.create_for despite the comment promising automatic reduction": 0.7598932981491089, "If OptimizedImage.downsize fails and returns false, the loop keeps retrying and the oversized file continues": 0.8418267965316772}